00:37:07.582 --> 00:37:22.458
Mythology with Dionysus and these rituals and traditions that we have, that it all comes back how our psyche functions. That means observing these external things gives us an idea and impression about how we work internally.

00:37:24.890 --> 00:37:43.753
And Jung mentioned mandalas, and this is a very big part of Jungian thought and ideas about the Self, because a mandala is always a circle. And Jung sees this, again, circle expressed in many, many different ways, in symbolism and imagery, but again, also in behavior. Not only in human beings.

00:37:44.267 --> 00:38:08.109
He writes, when a herd of elephants are frightened, they push the females and the little ones inside, and the males, the warriors, are outside. That is the most natural way of performing a protective mandala. This again mirrors what he described before about the dances of the primitive tribes. Warriors outside, children inside, a protective circle.

00:38:08.655 --> 00:38:30.067
And the mandala itself also is a protective circle in the psyche. He says when people are in a huge distress and they find their lives very, very chaotic, the psyche sends a kind of symbol to reassure them that a structure and an order is possible. And he says that's the mandala. And there's really different kind of mandalas.

00:38:30.340 --> 00:38:51.292
We know them mostly as pictures, as I have it here, as a round circle with like circles and areas inside and can also be square. But Jung says that's not the only way how to conceptualize a mandala, but rather a mandala is also acted out outside through behavior. This is what this quote is about.

00:38:51.933 --> 00:39:15.907
It is surely a mandala, and that always means a protective circle against the surrounding fire, against that thing which mixes one up with worldly events or with the bewildering facts of one's surroundings, which sweeps one along in a stampede, for instance. Again, we draw psychologically boundaries where you say, this is us, this is not us.

00:39:17.101 --> 00:39:23.218
And this creates a safe area. Area in which we operate, and Jung calls that consciousness.

00:39:25.220 --> 00:39:43.184
And what we try to do, we try to bring in all these things that are good and positive from the unconscious, but also to keep out the bad things, the overwhelming emotions and instincts that they're kind of there and integrated in a positive way, but they do not take over the ship, let's say. Similar with a garden, right?

00:39:43.506 --> 00:39:59.226
A garden, is a piece of cultivated land, meaning I have a border around it, I have a wall, and inside everything is structured to a certain, let's say, hierarchy or order. And Jung says this is what we try to do in our psyche.

00:39:59.611 --> 00:40:22.554
We build our consciousness, we develop to then bring in all those unconscious contents, all these ideas in a harmonious positive manner. And Jung says this is so fundamental in our psyche that even blind people know this. So this is what this quote about. I don't know how a blind person dreams of mandalas.

00:40:23.327 --> 00:40:45.060
Mandalas are also formed with the hands, danced, and depicted in music. When a mandala is created, all the circular and square forms known to humans play a part in it. So we act out mandalas. And if you want to find mandalas in your own dreams, It's then very important. It can be very imagistic.

00:40:45.189 --> 00:41:08.933
It can be as a picture is here, but really pay attention to things that are in a circle or they move in a circle. That took me also quite some time to find out because Jung talks about it at the very end of some seminar that it is not not only a circle itself, but it's moving.

00:41:09.403 --> 00:41:31.769
Mandalas are moving. And that already helps to recognize a lot of them. So what is like a very big psychological movement that's happening within us? Jung sees the psyche as structured very, very much. And there is a center point to our psyche and to our acting. And that is the Self.

00:41:32.262 --> 00:41:52.028
So we as the ego, as you can see here in this, in this diagram, we are on a path around the Self. And the interesting thing about the Self is the Self is actually us if we would have integrated everything that is us. So how we are right now is not how we will be in the future.

00:41:52.092 --> 00:42:15.191
We will be more in the future and like the ultimate endpoint of everything that could be us. Is the Self. And he describes that, that the ego is kind of circling around the Self. So self-knowledge reveals the fact that the soul's natural movement is not in a straight line, unless indeed it have undergone some deviation.

00:42:15.544 --> 00:42:37.826
On the contrary, it circles around something interior, around the center. And also from him and his own experiences from his life, During those years between 1918 and 1920, I began to understand that the goal of psychic development is the Self. There is no linear evolution. There's only a circumambulation of the Self.

00:42:39.626 --> 00:43:00.314
Meaning the journey that we have psychologically in our life and the actions that we do, it revolves around a point. And this point, we are not necessarily aware about. We kind of have to pay attention and be conscious of that, that what we do points to something.

00:43:00.667 --> 00:43:20.891
There's a commonality at its core, and we're going around it, and we kind of have to bring this forth. We, we kind of birth the Self through our actions, through the process of individuation, and enrich it with energy through our actions. And consciously bringing there something forth. And this, this is what I find so cool.

00:43:20.940 --> 00:43:43.268
